title: Decisions + Visual proposed-changes — design locked (THE LIGHTBOX)
summary: 'Founder-approved design for the next Conductor feature: a two-pronged answer to "reduce the walls of text" — (1) DECISIONS (agent offers options → human selects/types/chats, rendered as inline cards that drive the first-class needs-you amber) and (2) VISUAL proposed-changes ("THE LIGHTBOX", a canvas drawer that slides over the CHORUS rail; mermaid flows + comparison tables in v1). Verified mechanism: agent emits custom fenced blocks (mermaid/svg/conductor-decision/conductor-visual) + a per-session concision system prompt via --append-system-prompt; native AskUserQuestion surfaces cleanly but is unanswerable headless, so we use the fenced-block convention; answer = a normal text turn. MVP locked; building now.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#claude-stream-session'
  - '#conversation-model'
  - '#atrium-thread'
  - '#session-derived-status'
symbols_created:
  - '#fenced-block-parser'
  - '#agent-decision'
  - '#agent-visual'
  - '#atrium-decision-card'
  - '#atrium-visual-canvas'
  - '#session-prompt'
  - $decision-exchange
decisions:
  - id: TD-bridge-dec-001
    decision: Decisions + visuals ride on host-defined FENCED-BLOCK conventions (conductor-decision/conductor-visual/mermaid/svg) + a per-session concision system prompt via --append-system-prompt; do NOT depend on native AskUserQuestion.
    rationale: Empirically AskUserQuestion surfaces as a clean tool_use but auto-dismisses/is unanswerable headless. Fenced blocks ride verified text in/out, give host control, answer = normal text turn via existing send().
  - id: TD-bridge-dec-002
    decision: MVP = concision prompt + option-card decisions (amber→teal on commit, drives first-class needs-you) + mermaid flow + comparison table. Defer wireframes, A/B/C/D layout, diffs, animations.
    rationale: 'North: ~90% of agent→human moments with least rendering surface. Mermaid WebView is the v1 spike; cards+comparison ship even if it slips.'
  - id: TD-bridge-dec-003
    decision: Visuals live in THE LIGHTBOX — a canvas drawer sliding OVER the CHORUS rail (Chorus stays live underneath), invite-don't-impose; decisions are inline turns-that-ask-back, composer never locks.
    rationale: 'Mika: never trade live-agent visibility for a diagram; never re-create walls-of-text inline. Amber→teal on commit = the signature held-breath→exhale reserved for deciding.'
learnings:
  - 'AskUserQuestion headless: surfaces as a clean tool_use {questions:[{question,header,multiSelect,options:[{label,description}]}]} but auto-dismisses before a host can answer (''the prompt was dismissed''). Use a host-defined fenced-block decision convention; answer = normal text user turn.'
  - System-prompt injection for spawned claude -p = --append-system-prompt (NOT --system-prompt, which replaces the default and strips the agentic tools the cockpit reads). Per-process, invisible to the repo.
  - The real 'reduce walls of text' lever is PROMPTING (lead-with-answer, one-rec, ~6 lines then stop-or-block, caveats exempt) + structured renderable blocks. Block is canonical; prose must not contradict it.
  - 'Streaming-safe fenced-block parsing: parse the ACCUMULATED message text (applyAssistant accumulates), emit a block only on its CLOSING fence; tolerate malformed (degrade to code block); stable identity by id/ordinal; preserve a chosen answer across re-parse.'
tags:
  - conductor
