  - reduce-walls-of-text
  - design-locked
body: 'Two-pronged founder ask: (1) handle decisions (options→select/type/chat), (2) render visual proposed-changes to kill walls of text. Approved "in theory"; founder noted the meta-payoff: once built, plans render to him as diagrams+concise text. Designs: Arky (architecture: --append-system-prompt, FencedBlockParser, ConversationMessage.decisions/visuals, answerDecision reuses send(), pending-decision→noteNeedsHuman()→awaitingYou amber, MermaidWebView sandboxed+vendored-offline; file plan phases 0-4). Mika (THE LIGHTBOX slide-out over CHORUS; decision = amber-rail turn with stacked cards, ★ lean, ▸ look-closer; amber→teal on commit→collapse to ''✓ you chose B''; hover-option-highlights-diagram; diff teal/inkMuted; one amber per conversation). North (prose-by-default heuristic; taxonomy cards/mermaid/diff/wireframe/prose; concision contract; risk = brevity eating nuance → caveats exempt, confidence line, block canonical). Scholar authored the canonical --append-system-prompt copy (bridgeConventions: concision + block conventions + when-relevant gate). OWNERSHIP: Scholar owns the prompt copy; Swift owns the Swift; Mika sign-off on card+canvas; Loid loops decision answers + block counts as calibration signals.'
